00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:06.520
And if so, how did this come about?

441
00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:09.920
Well, we asked Matt Sohn about this, and here's what he had to say.

442
00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:18.760
On a fun side note, Phil Shea, our prop master, again, scored for us.

443
00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:27.800
He was able to get Nespresso to sign off and let us use one of their actual machines and their name,

444
00:20:28.060 --> 00:20:31.720
